{"kind":"assert","text":"DX-A2 wire adopted for the isolated implementation: ReadMinimum is { at: ScopeRef, head: number | Head }. A sequence minimum is incarnation-qualified, and a full head adds its exact hash; Head and FactRef stay closed. The five read methods take the same optional trailing minimum; HTTP carries one bounded canonical base64url query value, outside the existing application-projection payload.\n\nA dedicated behind result is { ok: false, reason: behind, current: FactRef }, including on applicationProjection. HTTP uses 503. Bounds.readWaitMilliseconds is 1,000, below the existing 10-second projection and 30-second ordinary HTTP limits. A reached full-head minimum succeeds only when its recorded hash matches; missing retained proof or mismatch uses existing unavailable. Wrong incarnation refuses without waiting, and a minimum for another scope or kind is invalid for that read. Authorization precedes any head exposure and is checked again after waiting. The bounded wait uses the post-seal hook outside turns and transactions, with a recheck after registration to prevent a missed wake. No new rate policy or polling protocol is introduced.\n\nSource work is isolated at .builder-worktrees/dx-a2-minimum-head-20261030 from Main 5dc9765f; the shared main checkout remains fixed for J4.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"planner"}}